FOR THE EAST PARK GREENWAY UNDERPASS AND DRAINAGE PLAN
1.
Parties. The parties to this Amendment No. 1 are the City of Cheyenne, on behalf of the
Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization, hereinafter referred to as the “MPO,” and
Summit Engineering, hereinafter referred to as the “Consultant.” The parties entered into a
Professional Services Agreement originally dated September 28, 2020.
2.
Purpose ofAmendment. The work for the East Park GreenwayUnderpass and Drainage Plan
has progressed as intended and on schedule, however, a desired project element has been
identified as a critical addition to the success ofthis plan. This Amendment No. I will include
additional professional services to complete a hydraulic modeling of the Union Pacific
Railroad (UPRR) embankment, provide 35% grading design for the Laramie County
Conservation District (LCCD), and develop a 35% Greenway plan and profile south of the
UPRR.
3.
Term. This Amendment No. I is effective upon approval and execution by the parties and
shall remain in effect through the ending date of the underlying Professional Services
Agreement.
4.
Amendment. The parties agree that the Professional Services Agreement is amended to
include
the
“Supplemental
Task
1:
Hydraulic
Modeling
Downstream
of UPRR
Embankment,” “Supplemental Task 2: 35% Grading Design for LEADS owned, Laramie
County Conservation District (LCCD) Open Space,” and “Supplemental Task 3: 35%
Greenway Plan and Profile,” attached hereto as Exhibit A and incorporated by reference.
5.
Compensation. In consideration ofthe services to be performed pursuant to this Amendment
No. 1, MPO shall pay the Consultant a “not-to-exceed” fee of$20,040.00. The total contract
amount shall not exceed $88,070.00.
6.
Force and Effect of Original Provisions. All other provisions of the original Professional
Services Agreement remain unchanged and continue to have full force and effect for the term
of the Professional Services Agreement.
