EXHIBITA
SUMMIT
/‘%ENCINEERING
May5,2021
Jillian Harris
Sr. Transportation Planner
Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization
615 West 20th Street
Cheyenne, WY 82001
RE: Proposal for Additional Services for East Park Greenway Underpass & Drainage Plan at the Union
Pacific Railroad
The purpose of this letter is to outline the scope of work and fee proposal for additional services desired
for the East Park Greenway Underpass & Drainage Plan at the Union Pacific Railroad.
GLM Design Group will provide Engineering Services for the hydraulic modeling
downstream of the UPRR Embankment. This modelling will take into account the
additional flow coming out of East Park from the proposed drainage culverts, as the
proposed culverts will convey more storm water than the existing historic arch
structure. The hydraulic and hydrologic analysis will also take into consideration the
existing low spot on Campstool Road, west of the Dry Creek culverts, that currently
serves as the spillway for high flows. This location will need to be included in the model
and alternative solutions proposed to ensure that the amount of storm water that
reaches lnterstate-80 is no higher than existing flows. Modeling will be done using City
of Cheyenne GIS contour data.
35% Preliminary Grading Plan for LEADS owned, Laramie County Conservation District
Open Space (LCCD)
Provide Engineering Services for a 35% grading design of the LCCD open space to
coincide with the results of the hydraulic and hydrologic modeling referenced as Part 1.
Grading design will be done with consideration given to the LCCD Master Plan including
wetland ponds and planned improvements to the site including the Black Hills Energy
electric transmission lines and towers.
307-637-0681
Hydraulic Modeling Downstream of UPRR Embankment
Fee $11,040
Dear Ms. Harris:
SCOPE OF SERVICES
PART 1
PART 2
5907 Townsend Place
Cheyenne, WY 82009
