### Page 12 of 14

```text
Exhibit A
Scope of Work
for
EAST PARK GREENWAY AND DRAINAGE PLAN AT UPRR
SCOPE OF WORK
— This scope of work outlined below summarizes the proposed scope from Summit
Engineering dated August 25, 2020. The Summit Engineering written proposal and this following scope
outline constitutes the entire scope of work for this Agreement.
TASK 1— KICK-OFF, PROJECT ADMINISTRATION, AND MEETINGS
Summit Engineering will conduct a kick-off meeting to gain a better understanding of the project goals
and expected outcome. Summit Engineering will conduct monthly project meetings and Steering
Committee Meetings. Summit Engineering will provide the MPO with agendas and meeting notes/minutes
for all meetings. Summit Engineering will meet with various project stakeholders including the Laramie
County Conservation District (LCCD), Mary Winkler, and Cheyenne Parks and Recreation Department as
necessary throughout the project.
Deliverables - Meeting agendas and minutes
SUBCONSULTANT TASKS
-
Martin-Martin: Structural investigation of the existing masonry culvert to determine the
structural integrity for use as a Greenway underpass.
•
Deliverables
— Structural investigation report and cost estimate for necessary
repairs.
-
Lithos Engineering: Recommendations for best tunneling practices including sizes of
potential borings thru the UPRR Embankment in coordination with GLM Design Group for
sizes and locations.
Lithos will provide
a concise tunneling feasibility memorandum
specifically discussing installation methods, risks and limitations, construction constraints,
and layout considerations.
•
Deliverables
— Tunnel feasibility memorandum and engineer’s estimate of
probable construction cost for proposed tunnel crossing(s).
360 Rail Services: Coordination and contact with the UPRR to introduce the project to them.
A 10% design plan will be given to the UPRR to show use of existing masonry arch structure
as the Greenway underpass and additional borings thru the UPRR embankment to convey
stormwater. Included in the UPRR submittal will be a description of the existing hydraulics
and the proposal for a berm to remove stormwater from being stored against their
embankment. The goal of this task is to have written correspondence from the UPRR
indicating that they view this project favorably for future construction.
•
Deliverables — Correspondence log with UPRR.
GLM Design Group: Recommendations for potential project funding of future construction
project.
•
Deliverables — Written report identifying funding sources and required next steps
to secure funding.
1
